      "narrative": "Mara's jaw tightens. She doesn't look away, but something shifts behind her eyes \u2014 a door opening.\n\n\"The passage wasn't council-sanctioned, if that's what you're thinking. It was off the books. Bram handled every crossing himself, but he didn't work alone.\" She leans in, voice barely a murmur now. \"The woman who sold the passage \u2014 who took the coin, kept the ledger, arranged the schedules \u2014 was a courier named **Sable Quill**. Travel-stained cloak, always coming or going. She worked the Copper Finch as her base. Had a room upstairs for years.\"\n\nMara's gaze flicks toward the stairs at the back of the tavern.\n\n\"She vanished the same night Bram died. No one's seen her since.\"\n\nToran shifts uncomfortably, his ink-stained fingers worrying the edge of his papers. \"I... I saw her that evening. She was at the bar, arguing with someone. A man in a hood. I didn't get a good look at his face, but I remember his voice \u2014 low, like gravel rolling downhill. He kept saying the Gate needed to stay *open*. That closing it would be a mistake.\"\n\nHe looks at you, pale. \"That was hours before Bram's body was found.\""
    },
