      "narrative": "The word hangs in the damp air, swallowed by the silence.\n\n\"Bram!\"\n\nYour voice echoes off the surrounding buildings, then fades into nothing. The grey sky presses down. The cobbles gleam with moisture. The Ash Gate stands\u4e0d\u52a8 \u2014 a slab of darkness that drinks the sound.\n\nNo answer comes from the Gate. No whisper, no footstep, no shift in the shadows behind the arch.\n\nThe cloaked woman stirs.\n\nShe turns her head slowly, and beneath the hood you catch the glint of eyes \u2014 dark, assessing, unwelcoming. Her voice is low, roughened by travel and disuse.\n\n\"He's not here.\"\n\nShe says it flatly. Not a question. A statement of fact.\n\n\"I've been sitting at this Gate for three days. No one passes through. No one passes back. No voices come from the other side.\"\n\nShe shifts, and the travel-stained cloak falls open slightly, revealing a leather satchel strapped across her chest \u2014 the kind couriers use for sealed documents.\n\n\"You knew him?\"\n\nThe question lands like a stone dropped into still water."
    },
